Gravitone builds on Pocket TTS as a dependency (installed via pip); it is
not vendored into this repository. Its license terms are unchanged and
apply to that component.

Voice assets carry PER-VOICE licenses — see
https://huggingface.co/kyutai/tts-voices. Only ship voices you have the
right to, and only clone a voice with the speaker's consent (see the Pocket
TTS "Prohibited use" section).

Why this text is here and not in LICENSE: GitHub detects a repository's
license by matching LICENSE against known license bodies. An attribution
paragraph inserted into the MIT text drops the match below the detection
threshold, and the repository then reports no license at all — which is
exactly what happened before this file existed. LICENSE stays verbatim MIT;
attribution lives here and in README.md.
